(The definitive proof of LunarSafe's physical validity lies in uncertainty enclosure: for all evaluated landing sites, the difference between computed mean) Tj
T* (slope and published benchmark slope falls within the analytical 2-sigma uncertainty envelope: |S_computed - S_published| <= 2 * sigma_S. Specifically:) Tj
T* (Apollo 11 error 0.08° <= 0.84° \(2*sigma\); Shiv Shakti error 0.33° <= 1.41° \(2*sigma\); and Shackleton error 1.42° <= 1.76° \(2*sigma\). Thus, all observed) Tj
T* (errors are mathematically accounted for by sensor precision.) Tj
